      "writtenOn": "2021-07-26T15:47:36Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We just switched compiler stack for Dawn from SPIRV-Cross to Tint:\n\n\u003e They are using some SPIRV instructions that aren\u0027t handled by Tint\u0027s SPIRV-Reader: runtime_intrinsics_matrix and runtime_intrinsics_trig.\n\u003e See https://bugs.chromium.org/p/tint/issues/detail?id\u003d1044 and https://bugs.chromium.org/p/tint/issues/detail?id\u003d1045",
      "parentUuid": "28593bbb_e0024572",
      "revId": "b2b1c8e986109e2d7c63262a7c57cb141aa950f6",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "8db1fd67_a15ec311",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 11059
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-07-26T15:50:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This would be a separate regression from either of those two bugs. It\u0027s failing to compare one matrix to another matrix, and failing to cast a mat2 to a vec4. One sec, I\u0027ll find you the SPIR-V we generate for those things.",
      "parentUuid": "218739f3_0814a6b9",
      "revId": "b2b1c8e986109e2d7c63262a7c57cb141aa950f6",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e45f8b8e_fe3290b7",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 11059
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-07-26T15:53:18Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This SPIR-V is slightly different from what you will actually receive because it\u0027s compiled in a stand-alone way (no actual GPU is set up), but it should be accurate for the stuff that matters.\n\nMatrixToVectorCast: https://osscs.corp.google.com/skia/skia/+/main:tests/sksl/shared/MatrixToVectorCast.asm.frag\n\nMatrixEquality: https://osscs.corp.google.com/skia/skia/+/main:tests/sksl/shared/MatrixEquality.asm.frag",
      "parentUuid": "8db1fd67_a15ec311",
      "revId": "b2b1c8e986109e2d7c63262a7c57cb141aa950f6",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d7c30ffb_6f073365",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 11059
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-07-26T16:06:24Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "(FWIW, it\u0027s probably worth mentioning that Skia went for a very long time without properly supporting either of these operations at all in SPIR-V, and in practice we got away with it. Comparing two matrices for equality is not very useful; casting mat2s to vec4s and back is more of a parlor trick than anything else. We support it because GLSL does. We allow users to submit arbitrary shaders, and so we want to be as GLSL-compatible as we can be. We have tests for it because our code generators have dedicated code to handle these operations. But I would 100% be willing to believe that outside of these particular Skia tests, none of Dawn\u0027s clients ever exercise these code paths.)",
      "parentUuid": "e45f8b8e_fe3290b7",
      "revId": "b2b1c8e986109e2d7c63262a7c57cb141aa950f6",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
